UID:event_316918727@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261024T043011Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261107T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261107T153000
SUMMARY:Scenic AVL - Camino Primitivo - with WNC American Pilgrims
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**Overview:** This hike is offered
  as a monthly training hike with the WNC Asheville Chapter of American Pil
 grims on the Camino. The route has been announced on the [Facebook Group P
 age](https://www.facebook.com/groups/AVLCamino/announcements).\nIf you are
  unfamiliar with the Camino\, here are a few links to learn more:\n[Americ
 an Pilgrims on the Camino](https://americanpilgrims.org/iwpmap_directory/w
 estern-north-carolina/)\n[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Way_(2010_film
 )](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Way_(2010_film))\nThis route is inspi
 red by the Camino Primitivo\, which has more hills than most of the other 
 routes to Santiago de Compostela.\n\n**Start:** 9:00 AM. Please arrive 10 
 minutes early.\n**Meeting Place:** Ingles\, 915 Merrimon Ave at the corner
  of Beaverdam Rd\; meet in the corner of the parking lot near the Ingles s
 ign and near Beaverdam Rd. Restrooms are available.\n**Full Distance:** 10
 .7 miles\n**Shorter Options:** 6\, 7\, or 8 miles\n**Elevation Gain:** 156
 0 feet\n**Duration:** Allow 6 hours with lunch stop\n**Hike Leader:** Maur
 ice Frank\n**Overview:**\nThis challenging high elevation gain walk is ins
 pired by the Camino Primitivo. We begin and end at Ingles on Merrimon Aven
 ue and Beaverdam Rd.\nOur first stage is a warm up on rolling hills throug
 h the beautiful heavily wooded Sherwood Heights neighborhood. Crossing ove
 r via Windsor Rd we reach the Reynolds Mountain community. We stop to rest
 \, hydrate and have a snack.\nIn the next section we steeply ascend up and
  around the top with beautiful long-range views. After lunch at The Villag
 e Porch in Reynolds Mountain we return around the back of Beaver Lake.\nTh
 ere are several options for a shorter less strenuous walk of about 6\, 7\,
  or 8 miles. The Sherwood Heights hills are moderate and you can skip the 
 climb up Reynolds Mountain.\nThere is no coffee stop along the route\, and
  no actual restrooms. We pass porto potties outside homes being renovated 
 or constructed.\nAlmost all of the route is on pavement. Wear appropriate 
 shoes and being snacks and water.\n\n**Guests:** For this hike\, there are
  no guest restrictions. Bring them with you.\n\n**Disclaimer and Release o
 f Liability:**\nThis activity involves hiking on city streets that may hav
 e traffic and/or hiking on natural surfaces. Participants are responsible 
 for their safety on streets and trails. The organizer of this trip is a vo
 lunteer and not a professional guide. The function of the organizer is onl
 y to organize this trip. If you sign up or participate in this event you a
 cknowledge that you freely and voluntarily agree to assume all risks of in
 juries\, illnesses\, and damages arising from\, as a result of\, and assoc
 iated with this event. You are responsible for any guests\, dogs or other 
 companions you bring with you. In addition\, you acknowledge that you agre
 e to the Meetup terms: [https://www.meetup.com/terms](https://www.meetup.c
 om/terms)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/316918727
 /
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261010T003048Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261010T003048Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncarboretum": "https://ncarboretum.org/event/landscape-photography-workshop/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncarboretum
X-SOURCE:NC Arboretum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261107T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261107T120000
DTSTAMP:20261001T180852Z
CREATED:20261001T180852Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261001T180852Z
UID:1778780020219-1794042000-1794052800@ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:Seeing Light: Landscape Photography at the North Carolina Arboretum
DESCRIPTION:Seeing Light: Landscape Photography at the North Carolina Arboretum\nwith Joseph Prater \nSaturday\, November 7  |  9 am – 12 pm \nRegister Here!\nParticipants will explore the Arboretum while learning the fundamentals of landscape photography\, including exposure\, composition\, working with natural light\, and recognizing compelling scenes. Instruction is entirely field-based and welcomes photographers of all experience levels\, including those using smartphones. \nThis program will take place outside and will follow easy trails and paved walkways. Dress for the weather and prepare to be outside for the entire program time. \nJoey Prater is a North Carolina-based landscape photographer whose work is inspired by the mountains\, forests\, and changing seasons of the Southeast. With a lifelong love of the outdoors and years spent exploring public lands\, he enjoys creating images that showcase both the beauty and character of wild places. Joey is passionate about sharing his knowledge with photographers of all experience levels\, helping others build confidence while developing their own creative vision. His goal is to inspire people to slow down\, explore with intention\, and experience a deeper connection with the landscapes around them. \n●  Members: Remember to enter your promo code upon checkout to receive your 10% member discount! Email adulteducation@ncarboretum.org with questions. \n●  See a full listing of Adult Education Programs at the North Carolina Arboretum here! Questions? Check our FAQs. \n●  We are committed to fostering a diverse\, supportive learning community. If the cost of a class is a barrier for you\, please complete this scholarship form and we will see what kind of assistance we can provide. \n●  Follow us on Facebook & Instagram! \n●  Join our Adult Education Student Hub on Discord! \n●  Interested in supporting the NC Arboretum more directly? Donate to the ONE Fund here. \nSee all of our classes open for registration here!
URL:https://ncarboretum.org/event/landscape-photography-workshop/
CATEGORIES:Adult Education
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/joseph-prater-landscape-photography.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ashevilleart": "https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/the-art-of-presence-meditation-and-reflection-in-the-museum-3/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ashevilleart
X-SOURCE:Asheville Art Museum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261107T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261107T110000
DTSTAMP:20260914T153405Z
CREATED:20260604T193254Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260914T153405Z
UID:10006747-1794043800-1794049200@www.ashevilleart.org
SUMMARY:The Art of Presence: Meditation and Reflection in the Museum
DESCRIPTION:Step into the Museum’s galleries before the doors open for a quiet and contemplative morning of meditation\, mindful walking\, and reflection. This guided experience invites participants to slow down\, settle the nervous system\, and explore the Museum as a place of sanctuary\, spaciousness\, and renewal. \nThe session will begin with a brief seated meditation\, followed by a walking meditation through selected exhibits. Along the way\, participants will pause with gentle mindfulness prompts designed to support personal reflection\, embodied awareness\, and a deeper connection with the artwork. Rather than offering art historical interpretation\, the experience encourages each participant to notice what arises within them through presence\, stillness\, and mindful seeing. The group will honor noble silence throughout much of the session with occasional opportunities for brief reflection and sharing. No previous meditation experience is needed. \nJoin Joshua on 8/22\, 10/3\, 11/7\, and 12/5. \nJoshua Canter is a mindfulness meditation teacher and the founder of True Nature Travels and Education\, an Asheville-based organization that has offered transformative retreats and educational experiences around the world for more than 20 years. He holds a master’s degree in Contemplative Psychology and is passionate about making mindfulness accessible\, grounded\, and relevant to everyday life. \nPurchase Tickets \nPlease enter through the Staff Entrance to the left of the building.
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/the-art-of-presence-meditation-and-reflection-in-the-museum-3/
LOCATION:Asheville Art Museum\, 2 South Pack Square\, Asheville\, NC\, 28801\, United States
CATEGORIES:Wellness
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://www.ashevilleart.org/wp-content/uploads/Screenshot-2026-03-31-at-1.17.55-PM-scaled.png
GEO:35.5946714;-82.5512827
