X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Jack of the Wood": "https://jackofthewood.com/events/jackson-grimms-old-time-machine/", "Where Y'at AVL Music": "https://jackofthewood.com/events/jackson-grimms-old-time-machine/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Jackofthewood Events Ics": "https://jackofthewood.com/events/jackson-grimms-old-time-machine/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:jackofthewood_events_ics
X-SOURCE:Jack of the Wood, Where Y'at AVL Music
UID:12223@jackofthewood.com
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261121T203000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261121T233000
DTSTAMP:20260917T182032Z
URL:https://jackofthewood.com/events/jackson-grimms-old-time-machine/
SUMMARY:Jackson Grimm's Old Time Machine
DESCRIPTION:\nJackson Grimm marries folk pop melodies with the lonesome sou
 nd of traditional Appalachian music. In a region with a strong music cultu
 re\, it is no surprise that Grimm's songwriting is representative of his m
 usical birthplace: Asheville\, NC.&nbsp\;\n\n\n\nHis Appalachian-infused A
 mericana songs run the gamut from a traditional country waltz homage ("If 
 Not For You") to an unrequited love song driven by a&nbsp\;Beatles-esque m
 elody&nbsp\;("I'd Hold You\, But I Don't Wanna Hold You)" to a drunken Old
  Crow Medicine Show-style partygrass number ("Last Train Home").\n\n\n\nGr
 imm studied Traditonal Music at Warren Wilson College under the tutelage o
 f renowned players like Wayne Erbsen and Kevin Kehrberg. He also studied g
 uitar\, banjo\, mandolin &amp\; singing&nbsp\;with the Western North Carol
 ina music master\, Josh Goforth.\n\n\n\nHe also plays extensively as a sid
 eman for his father\, singer-songwriter Tim Grimm\, touring all over the U
 S and to Europe. Jackson has appeared on\, written songs on\, and co-produ
 ced the last two Tim Grimm albums.&nbsp\;He's&nbsp\;has also shared the st
 age and played with singer-songwriters Ben Bedford\, Krista Detor\, Jennie
  DeVoe &amp\; Old Sap.\n\n\n\nStill a hometown boy\, Grimm can be found pl
 aying solo or around Western North Carolina with Holler Choir\, One Strin
 gband\, or his Old Time Machine.\n\n\n\nMusic 8:30-11:30pm\, $10 cover at 
 the door.\n\n\n\n\nhttps://youtu.be/24cT03q0IT8\n\n\n\n\n\nhttps://youtu.b
 e/Lu8H1TbBxaQ\n\n\n\n\n\nhttps://youtu.be/0_4HeoySPyw\n\n
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://jackofthewood.com/wp-content/uploads/202
 6/05/Jacksongrimm1.jpeg
END:VEVENT
